laurel 2972: CPU governor: a core full for one tick goes to its cap; touch holds both caps, GPU work holds Gold's

Owner 2026-11-03: use all CPU cores fully. [V boot 11] Under load both clusters read the top row for all 60 s, so the cap never held a loaded core; the loss is at the edges.
From idle a load waited 120 ms for the top row (80 ms below it, at 300-650 MHz of 2016) [V gov-test before this patch]. While the UI moved Gold spent 14 s a minute at 1401-1804 MHz [V CPUFREQ lines 00:55-00:57], and touches held Silver at 1305 MHz.
Line: LAUREL CPUFREQ: on: OSM governor ... Host test: scripts/laurel/gov-test.sh. Cost: more power; the thermal caps of 2303 still win.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/laurel_gov_core.h b/bsd/dev/laurel_gov_core.h
--- a/bsd/dev/laurel_gov_core.h
+++ b/bsd/dev/laurel_gov_core.h
@@ -2,27 +2,31 @@
  * laurel 2890: the OSM governor's one decision, without kernel types, so that the host test
  * (scripts/laurel/gov-test.sh) runs exactly this code. One step for one cluster.
  *   busy  % of the busiest core over the last LGOV_WINDOW ticks (LGOV_TICK_MS each)
+ *   tick  % of the busiest core over the last tick alone (laurel 2972)
  *   row   the row the cluster runs now; cap the thermal cap; floor the governor's lowest row (the cap wins)
  *   hold  a row wanted by the UI right now (touch, GPU work); 0 = none
  *   low   ticks in a row below LGOV_LO (kept by the caller)
  * Before 2890 [V 2303]: 100 ms tick, 300 ms window, > 90 %: cap, > 70 %: +1 row. A load that starts on an idle core reads
  * 33 %, 66 %, 100 %: the top row came 300 ms after the load, the first frames of a touch ran at 300 MHz.
+ * laurel 2972 (owner 2026-11-03: use all CPU cores fully): a core that was full for one tick goes to the cap at once: 40 ms from idle, not
+ * 120. Over those 80 ms the core runs at 300 to 650 MHz of 2016: 50 to 70 ms of work lost per burst [I].
  */
 #ifndef LAUREL_GOV_CORE_H
 #define LAUREL_GOV_CORE_H
 #define LGOV_TICK_MS    40u
 #define LGOV_WINDOW     3u
 #define LGOV_JUMP       85u     /* a core full for 120 ms: the cap at once */
+#define LGOV_JUMP_TICK  90u     /* laurel 2972: a core full for one tick: the cap at once */
 #define LGOV_HI         60u     /* +2 rows */
 #define LGOV_LO         30u
 #define LGOV_DOWN_TICKS 8u      /* 320 ms below LGOV_LO: -1 row (as before: about 300 ms) */
 
 static inline unsigned
-lgov_next(unsigned busy, unsigned row, unsigned floor, unsigned cap, unsigned hold, unsigned *low)
+lgov_next(unsigned busy, unsigned tick, unsigned row, unsigned floor, unsigned cap, unsigned hold, unsigned *low)
 {
 	unsigned want = row;
 
-	if (busy > LGOV_JUMP) {
+	if (busy > LGOV_JUMP || tick >= LGOV_JUMP_TICK) {
 		want = cap;
 		*low = 0;
 	} else if (busy > LGOV_HI) {
